  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kitui Home Based Care and Children&apos;s Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kitui Home based care and orphans programme has registered significant success in delivering services to people infected and affected by HIV and AIDS including orphans. Services were delivered through medical and nursing care, psychosocial and spiritual care, home visits, school health initiatives, and community mobilisatiion and sensitization. Among achievements realised during this period were improved health of clients using ARVs and those on treatment of opportunistic infections. A large number of beneficiaries were reached through peer education and community sensitisation by support groups of PLWHA. This has increased knowledge on HIV and AIDS among young people and the general population. 

An immediate concern is the growing number of children and young people living 
with HIV. They are faced with adolescence crisis compounded by their HIV status. They have limited skills to respond to their situation, and a well thought intervention to address their needs is necessary.

Collaboration with the Ministry of Health (MoH) in provision of health services to beneficiaries is commendable. MoH continues to support the diocesan interventions including secondment of staff, provision of drugs and supplies and staff capacity building. Partnerships with AIDS Population and Health Integrated Assistance (APHIA 2) Program funded by USAID have been strengthened. Increased networking with local civil society organisations and community participation and involvement are remarkable. Collaboration and networking has significantly strengthened the programme in terms of reach and improved service delivery.</narrative>
  </description>
